Upstream-Name: kitty
Upstream-Contact: Kovid Goyal <kovid@kovidgoyal.net>
Source: https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty
Comment:
 The binary packages repackage upstream's prebuilt Linux bundle, which
 contains kitty itself and statically bundled copies of its runtime: CPython
 (PSF-2.0), OpenSSL (Apache-2.0), HarfBuzz (MIT), FreeType (FTL or GPL-2),
 cairo (LGPL-2.1 or MPL-1.1), pixman (MIT), libpng (libpng-2.0), zlib (Zlib),
 brotli (MIT), lcms2 (MIT), xxHash (BSD-2-Clause), GLib (LGPL-2.1), graphite2
 (LGPL-2.1), libffi (MIT), expat (MIT), ncurses (MIT), readline (GPL-3),
 SQLite (public domain), wayland (MIT), libxkbcommon (MIT), xz (0BSD), bzip2
 (bzip2-1.0.6), libiconv (LGPL-2.1), the slang shader compiler (Apache-2.0
 with LLVM exception) and the Symbols Nerd Font Mono (MIT). Upstream publishes
 a full SPDX SBOM next to every release (kitty-<version>.tar.xz.spdx.json).

